# Vulnerabilities ignored by Trivy. Each entry must carry a reason.
# Revisit whenever the scan turns red: drop entries whose fixed package has
# landed in the Debian suite the runner image tracks (bookworm-security).

# Chromium vulnerabilities fixed upstream in 153.0.8010.36 and 153.0.8010.47.
# Debian uploaded the fixed source to bookworm-security as
# 153.0.8010.47-2~deb12u1, but its binaries have not been built yet, so
# bookworm-security still publishes 152.0.7977.82-1~deb12u1 on amd64 and arm64
# and `apt-get upgrade` in server/Dockerfile has no patched package to install.
# Pulling Chromium from trixie-security onto bookworm would replace hundreds of
# core packages including glibc.
# Chromium is present solely to render Open Graph images. It renders markup the
# server builds from fixed templates, with only server-signed, HTML-escaped text
# interpolated in and fonts inlined as data URIs. It never navigates to a remote
# page, loads no extensions, and shows no browser UI, so none of the crafted
# page, crafted extension, compromised renderer, or social engineering vectors
# these CVEs require are reachable. CVE-2026-87534, CVE-2026-87616,
# CVE-2026-91727, and CVE-2026-91748 also only affect Android, Windows, or macOS.
# Drop these entries once bookworm-security publishes 153.0.8010.47-2~deb12u1.
